description:
in repos/development-vessel/src/resolvers/feature-compose.ts, the `refute()` helper accepts a refutation on `rp.refuted === true`, `rp.confidence >= 0.8`, and `rp.reason.trim().length >= 20`, and never checks whether the reasoning agrees with the verdict. On 2026-08-28 a refuter emitted `refuted: true` at confidence 1.00 while its own reason said "the diff shows countLinesFromSource() is indeed called, thus the refutation is incorrect on that point. My apologies. Re-evaluating." It was counted toward the 2/2 quorum and rolled back a patch that had passed typecheck, shape-dispatch, the test suite, and the first judge.

Make exactly one edit, using the literal strings below. Both anchors occur exactly once in the file.

Replace this exact line:

        return { refuted: true, confidence: rp.confidence, reason: rp.reason.trim() };

with this exact block:

        // A refutation whose own reasoning withdraws it is not a refutation. Observed
        // 2026-08-28: a refuter emitted refuted:true at confidence 1.00 while its reason read
        // "...thus the refutation is incorrect on that point. My apologies. Re-evaluating."
        // and was still counted toward the quorum, rolling back a patch that had passed
        // typecheck, shape-dispatch, the test suite AND the first judge. The verdict field and
        // the reasoning it ships with must agree before the vote counts. Narrow by design: this
        // matches an EXPLICIT self-withdrawal, not hedging or uncertainty, because a vague
        // refutation is already the job of the confidence floor above.
        if (SELF_RETRACTION.test(rp.reason)) return null;
        return { refuted: true, confidence: rp.confidence, reason: rp.reason.trim() };

Then, immediately BEFORE this exact line (which also occurs exactly once, and is the line that opens the `refute` helper):

      const refute = async (): Promise<{ refuted: boolean; confidence: number; reason: string } | null> => {

insert this exact block:

      // Explicit self-withdrawal phrases. Kept as a named constant so the pattern is greppable
      // and testable rather than buried in a conditional.
      const SELF_RETRACTION =
        /\b(?:the\s+)?refutation\s+is\s+incorrect|\bi\s+(?:was|am)\s+(?:wrong|mistaken|incorrect)\b|\bmy\s+apologies\b|\bre-?evaluating\b|\bretract(?:ing|ion|ed)?\b|\bon\s+second\s+(?:thought|reading)\b/i;

Change nothing else. Do not touch the confidence floor, the length check, the 2-refuter quorum, the SPLIT branch, or the fail-open catch — all of those are deliberate and correct.

Preserve existing behaviour exactly: `test/resolvers/feature-compose-adversarial-quorum.test.ts` must keep passing. In particular its first case supplies the refutation reason "the diff only renames the local variable; process.env[\"WRITE_ALLOWLIST\"] and the env-gate are untouched, so the gap condition still holds on the live path", which contains no self-withdrawal phrase and must still flip the verdict to addresses:false.

The file must typecheck and the vessel test suite must show no newly failing tests.

